course: dictionary
lesson: 1642
title: One word, many meanings: chill
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words change meaning depending on the sentence around them. The word chill has several meanings, and the context tells you which one is right. «There was a chill in the air this morning» means a feeling of cold. Try cold in its place: it still makes sense.
explain: «Put the lemonade in the fridge to chill.» Here chill is a verb, and it means to make something cold. But «A chill ran down her spine» is different: a chill is a shiver of fear, not a cold day. Ask yourself what would fit in the sentence, then check your meaning.
explain: Chill also has an informal meaning in everyday talk. «Chill!» means «Calm down», and «chilling» means relaxing. When someone says «Your dads are so chill», they mean relaxed. «Chill out» and «calm down» mean the same thing.
fact: Chill can be a noun, a verb or an adjective.
fact: «A chill» can mean a feeling of cold, as in «a chill in the air», or a mild illness where you feel cold and shivery, as in «catch a chill».
fact: «To chill» means to make something cold or cool, often in a fridge. Chilling food slows down bacteria.
fact: «Wind chill» is how much colder the wind makes it feel.
fact: Informal: a chill person is relaxed, and «chill out» means calm down.
exercise: «There was a chill in the air as we left the house.» What does chill mean here? | A game played at school | *A feeling of cold | A hot wave of summer sun | A loud noise in the street
exercise: Dad says, «Put the lemonade in the fridge to chill.» What does chill mean? | To cook something in an oven | To shout very loudly | *To make something cold | To wash something clean
exercise: Your friend says «Chill!» when you are worried about the test. What does it mean? | *Calm down | Run faster | Go to bed early | Get colder
test: «A chill ran down her spine when she heard the creak on the stairs.» What does chill mean here? | A mild illness | Relaxing on the sofa | *A feeling of fear | A cold drink
test: Ella says, «Mum is so chill about homework.» What does chill mean? | Cold to touch | Angry | *Relaxed | Tired from walking
exam: «She went out without a coat and caught a chill.» What does catch a chill mean? | *A mild illness where you feel cold and shivery | To freeze a cup of tea | To make her coat colder | A game of hide and seek
